# MAP DATA LICENCES

The source code in this package is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). The map boundary
data is not — each country's data carries the licence of the source it was
derived from, listed below.

This split is normal for map libraries: using the package is unrestricted, but
redistributing or modifying the boundary data itself carries the obligations of
whichever source it came from.

## Nepal — src/countries/np/data/

Districts and provinces.

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Source: Sagarjkhatri, via Wikimedia Commons

CC BY-SA 4.0 is a share-alike licence: modified versions of this boundary data
must be distributed under the same terms, with attribution retained.

## India — src/countries/in/data/

States and union territories.

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Source: Census of India 2011

Share-alike, as with Nepal: modified versions of this boundary data must be
distributed under the same terms, with attribution retained.

Note for future data: Indian government open data is normally published under the
Government Open Data Licence - India (GODL-India), not a Creative Commons licence.
Datasets sourced from data.gov.in, Survey of India or Census of India portals
should be checked for GODL terms rather than assumed to be CC.

## Germany — src/countries/de/data/

Bundeslaender (states) and Kreise (districts).

Licence: Data licence Germany - Attribution - Version 2.0 (DL-DE/BY-2.0)
https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/by-2-0
Source: GeoBasis-DE / Bundesamt fuer Kartographie und Geodaesie (BKG),
obtained via the geoBoundaries project (https://www.geoboundaries.org/)

DL-DE/BY-2.0 requires attribution only - there is no share-alike obligation, so
derived works may be redistributed under any terms provided the source is named.

The geoBoundaries project additionally asks to be acknowledged where its data is
used, which is why it appears in the attribution overlay alongside BKG.

## Austria — src/countries/at/data/

Bundeslaender (states) and Bezirke (districts).

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Source: Colazivi, "AT - blank - all layers.svg", via Wikimedia Commons
